          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Agricultural Wisdom</strong><br>\nHesiod's \"Works and Days\" is valued for its agricultural wisdom. It is among the earliest known works that provide a farmer's almanac-like content, offering practical guidance for crop and livestock farming. His descriptions reflect the farming practices of his time and region, and his counsel on the best times for planting and harvesting remains influential.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Hesiod's Influence on Philosophy</strong><br>\nThe moral and practical teachings found in Hesiod's poetry influenced later Greek philosophers. His ideas about work, justice, and the divine order of the universe were reflected in the writings of Plato and others. Hesiod helped to shape the philosophical landscape of ancient Greece by blending everyday experience with theological and ethical reflections.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy and Historical Importance</strong><br>\nHesiod's works have stood the test of time and continue to be studied for their historical and literary value. They not only provide a window into ancient Greek life but also contribute to the understanding of human culture and thought. Hesiod's blend of practical, philosophical, and theological themes makes his works a lasting part of world literature.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
